[702.549395, "o", "print(\"threshold >12:\", run(base.replace('> 10', '> 12')))\r\n# control 3: threshold > 11 -> 12-student depts\r\nprint(\"threshold >11:\", run(base.replace('> 10', '> 11')))\r\n# control 4: ignore graduation dates -> counts change\r\nprint(\"no grad filter:\", run(base.replace('FILTER(!BOUND(?graduatedOn) || ?graduatedOn > \"2025-08-16\"^^xsd:date)', '')))\r\n# control 5: no role filter -> assistants included if they qualify\r\nprint(\"no rank filter:\", run(base.replace('FILTER(!REGEX(LCASE(?role), \"assistant|associate|adjunct|visiting|emeritus|lecturer|teaching\"))','')))\r\n# control 6: reference date before all graduations\r\nprint(\"today=2024-02-01:\", run(base.replace('2025-08-16', '2024-02-01')))\r\nEOF — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && python3 - <<'EOF' import sys, re sys.path.insert(0,'.tmp_ev…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 39 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ All clauses demonstrably filter (removing any one changes results). Now l…\r\n[approval] bash: cd /app && python3 .tmp_eval/sparql_eval.py university_graph.ttl solution.sparql && rm -rf .tmp_eval && ls -a /app && echo \"--- solution.sparql ---\" && cat solution.sparql — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash cd /app && python3 .tmp_eval/sparql_eval.py university_graph.ttl solut…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 40 tool call(s) so far\r\n`/app/solution.sparql` is written and verified.\r\n\r\n**What the query does** (reference date 2025-08-16):\r\n\r\n1. **Full professors** — `uni:role` contains \"professor\" but not `assistant|associate|adjunct|visiting|emeritus|lecturer|teaching`.\r\n2. **EU department** — a sub-select requiring at least one `worksIn` department whose `belongsTo` university has a `locatedInCountry` in an explicit `VALUES` list of the 27 ISO alpha-2 codes of EU member states as of 2025-08-16 (`GR` for Greece, etc.).\r\n3. **Big department** — a grouped sub-select per professor/department counting `COUNT(DISTINCT ?student)` over students enrolled in courses `isTaughtIn` that department, keeping only students enrolled on/before and not graduated by the reference date (`HAVING ... > 10`).\r\n4. The outer pattern walks every department the professor works in to build `GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?country; separator=\", \")`.\r\n\r\n**How it was checked:** no SPARQL engine, pip or network exists in this sandbox, so I wrote a throwaway minimal SPARQL 1.1 evaluator (BGP, OPTIONAL, FILTER, VALUES, sub-SELECT, GROUP BY/HAVING, COUNT DISTINCT, GROUP_CONCAT, ORDER BY), ran the actual query file against the Turtle, and then ran ablation controls to confirm no clause passes vacuously (removing the EU filter, the rank filter, or the graduation filter each changes the result; raising the threshold to `>12` empties it). Result:\r\n\r\n```\r\nAristotle Tympas   GR\r\nOrfeas Menis       GR, US\r\nPepe Attanasio     PT, GR\r\n```\r\n\r\nJohn Smith (US only), Marie Dubois (Sorbonne: 6 current students), and the two assistant professors are correctly excluded. The temporary evaluator was deleted; `/app` now holds only `solution.sparql` plus the original files.\r\n\r\nOne caveat: `GROUP_CONCAT` ordering is by spec undefined, so a `PT, GR` vs `GR, PT` difference is engine-dependent — the country *sets* are what the query guarantees.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=implementor model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=40 surface=59338fa2ec97\r\n"]
